## Problem

# `_b00t_/b00t-skill-improve-loop.hive.toml` exists but is not wired.
# `guard-violations.jsonl` is accumulating violations (visible in git status, modified).
# No automatic path from violation → diagnosis → tomllm patch → apply.

# Self-improvement requires operator (frontier-tier human) to manually:
# 1. Read guard-violations.jsonl
# 2. Identify patterns
# 3. Update datums or guards manually

# This is toil. It should be the loop's job.

## Finished State

# When hive profile `b00t-skill-improve-loop` is active:
# 1. sm0l reads `guard-violations.jsonl` → classifies violations by datum/guard rule
# 2. ch0nky proposes `.tomllm.delta` patch for each recurring violation pattern
# 3. frontier (or operator gate) validates patch before apply
# 4. `b00t datum patch` applies approved delta
# 5. OKR KR tracks: `wc -l guard-violations.jsonl` → target: 0 new violations/day

# Loop runs on schedule (cron or systemd timer) ONLY when:
# - `b00t hive status` confirms ch0nky VRAM is free (RTX3090 / 31GB gate)
# - No active `in-progress` tasks at frontier tier

## OKR Instance (dogfooding PRD-ARCH-001)

# ```toml
# [b00t]
# name = "okr-hive-self-improve"
# type = "okr"

# [okr]
# objective = "hive continuously reduces guard violations without operator intervention"
# owner = "b00t-skill-improve-loop"

# [[okr.kr]]
# id = "kr1"
# check = "tail -n 1 guard-violations.jsonl | jq '.timestamp' 2>/dev/null || echo none"
# description = "no new violations in last 24h"
# pass_pattern = "none"
# owner = "sm0l"
# status = "pending"

# [[okr.kr]]
# id = "kr2"
# check = "wc -l < guard-violations.jsonl"
# description = "violations file shrinks week-over-week"
# pass_pattern = "^[0-9]+$"  # sm0l checks trend, not absolute
# owner = "sm0l"
# status = "pending"
# ```

## Pipeline

# ```
# [cron/systemd] every 6h
#      │
#      ▼
# sm0l: b00t hive status                    # resource gate
#      │ if ch0nky VRAM free
#      ▼
# sm0l: parse guard-violations.jsonl        # classify violations → JSON
#      │ output: { violation_type, count, datum_ref }[]
#      ▼
# ch0nky: propose .tomllm.delta per type   # fix datum/guard causing violation
#      │ output: <violation-type>.tomllm.delta
#      ▼
# frontier/operator: review delta           # gate: require approval if complexity > 5
#      │ approve → apply
#      ▼
# sm0l: b00t datum patch <base> <delta>     # apply approved delta
#      │
#      ▼
# sm0l: b00t datum update okr-hive-self-improve okr.kr[0].status=pass
# ```

## Acceptance Criteria

# - [ ] `b00t-skill-improve-loop` hive profile activates without error
# - [ ] sm0l violation classifier runs against `guard-violations.jsonl` (schema: see existing file)
# - [ ] ch0nky generates at least 1 valid `.tomllm.delta` from real violations (dogfood test)
# - [ ] `b00t datum patch` applies delta without corruption (depends PRD-ARCH-002)
# - [ ] OKR datum `okr-hive-self-improve.tomllm` created and queryable
# - [ ] Loop respects resource gate: does NOT run when ch0nky is loaded

